    {
      "name": "GPIO23",
      "label": "GPIO23 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "23",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED (23u) — LED2, a real RP2350B silicon GPIO (distinct from LED1/LED_BUILTIN=pin 64, which is the RM2/CYW43 wireless chip's own WL_GPIO0). #define-only in this board's pins_arduino.h (no static-const alias — the D0-D22 sequence never revisits GPIO23), so not auto-swept by build_boards.js; added explicitly. Confirmed active-high via the official schematic PDF (GPIO23 -> 470R R22 -> LED anode -> cathode -> GND, net 'LED_GP23') and corroborated by github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-pico issue #3297 ('LED2 (GPIO23) ... turning off reliably when set LOW').\nCheck if available on board"
    },
